  "text": "Thermodynamics, energy transformations from one form into another under certain conditions. Chemical energy stored by molecules. Methane, cooking gas or coal, fuel. Fuel burns in air, heat, reactions, chemical. Fuel burns in an engine, work, mechanical. Galvanic cell, like dry cell, energy, electrical. Forms of energy interrelated, transformed from one form into another form. Thermodynamics, study of these transformations. Not how, not at what rate, based on initial state, final state. Laws deal with energy changes of a system undergoing the change macroscopic, a large number of molecules, rather than microscopic, a few molecules. Thermodynamics, study of these transformations, not how, not at what rate. Based on initial state, final state. Laws apply only when a system is in equilibrium or moves state to state. Equilibrium to equilibrium, pressure, temperature in equilibrium do not change. With thermodynamics, study of these transformations. Not how, not at what break. Based on initial state, final state.",
